<title>USA: GE names top educator to head GE Fund.</title>
<headline>GE names top educator to head GE Fund.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFIELD, Conn. 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Electric Co. said Thursday it named Dr. Dolores Cross, president of Chicago State University, as president of the GE Fund, the company's philanthropic arm.</p>
<p>The GE Fund is one of the biggest charitable foundations in the U.S.</p>
<p>Cross, 59, is credited with helping turn around the troubled Chicago State University, GE said. She is also among the relatively few African-American women to head a university.</p>
<p>Her appointment is effective October 1.</p>
<p>Cross succeeds Dr. Clifford V. Smith, Jr., who is retiring.</p>
<p>--Hartford newsroom (860) 727-0224</p>
